# cdz-syntax-consumer-guest is a SEPARATE, dependency-declaring wasm32 component crate whose build MUST
# be byte-reproducible (its lifted component is content-addressed; the CI + flake `wasm-tools component
# new` needs a stable output hash), and floating deps would break that. So we COMMIT this crate's
# Cargo.lock — un-ignore it here (scoped to this dir) — while still ignoring build output. `--locked`
# builds are then deterministic in CI + Nix.
!Cargo.lock
